36,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The financial data is revealing. Fixed costs are over 280,000 yen, and fuel contributions are very lopsided; two people paid for most of it, while one barely contributed. We definitely need a more balanced payment system.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,It seems the financial imbalance is only one part of the problem. My research suggests that the emotional toll of policing each other's figures can be quite damaging to the group's harmony.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The logistics are just as broken as the finances. I found that weekly repeating trips are frequently collapsing, and the car is often handed over with the fuel light on and rubbish inside. It's completely unreliable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The diary shows a huge gap in usage between weekdays and weekends, especially during holidays. Also, trying to track every single run is a nightmare—it takes nearly an hour a week just to manage the data.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found out that our heavy use comes in bursts, like moves or trips, and those weeks take up whole evenings just to coordinate. Also, the mechanic said short trips are harder on the car.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Minako,,"It's clear that our ""informal"" approach is failing. We have financial imbalances, logistical chaos, and a significant time burden just to manage the car. We need a system that removes the need for constant policing.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Minako. If checking figures creates resentment and constant coordination consumes our evenings, we must seek a solution that prioritizes autonomy and predictability over meticulous, manual accounting. We need a system that breathes.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"Predictability is exactly what's missing. If repeating trips are collapsing and the car is left in a mess, we need a system that assigns clear responsibility and ensures the vehicle is ready for the next person.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shion,,"If we want predictability, we can't rely on a manual diary that takes an hour a week to maintain. We need a system that doesn't require us to be accountants just to drive.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I agree. Spending whole evenings just to figure out who can drive when is exhausting. We need something that doesn't make us feel so stressed every time someone has a big trip.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Minako,,We have a clear picture now: the current guesswork is unfair and the coordination is exhausting. We need a system that balances the costs without making us police each other or waste our evenings.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. We must avoid a solution that transforms us into auditors. If the act of checking figures breeds accusation, then a system based on constant verification will only further erode our friendship.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. We need a system that guarantees the car is available for those essential weekly trips and ensures it's kept in a decent state, without requiring a constant, stressful negotiation every single morning.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Let's be realistic. We can't have a system that's both perfectly fair and effortless. If we want to stop the guesswork and the hour-long bookkeeping, we have to accept a simpler, more rigid structure.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just want something where we don't have to spend our whole night arguing or planning. If a simpler system means we can just relax and not worry about the coordination, I think that's better.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Minako,,"It seems we all agree that the current chaos is unsustainable. We need a balance between financial fairness, logistical reliability, and our own mental well-being. Let's look at the options and decide which one solves these issues best.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I believe we are now perfectly positioned to evaluate the options. Let us choose the path that preserves our peace of mind while resolving the practical failures of our current arrangement.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I'm ready to vote. We need a solution that eliminates the morning stress and the lack of accountability for the car's condition. Let's see which option actually provides that stability.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shion,,I'm ready too. Let's see which option actually cuts through the noise. I'm looking for something that stops the guesswork without turning us into full-time bookkeepers. Let's get to the voting.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm ready too. I just hope we pick something that lets us stop worrying so much about the planning. I'll vote for whatever makes things the most peaceful for everyone.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
